    pr_ref:  # 030a
    description: "The ObjC analyzer emits an imports edge only for #import, never for #include (objc.py, the preproc_include arm: \"Check if it's #import (not #include)\"). The restriction dates from the analyzer's first commit (d8252de120) with no reason recorded.\n\nFound by WI-somod. Before it, the C or C++ grammar also parsed every ObjC header and recorded its #include lines, so the gap was hidden for headers. Now each ObjC header is parsed by the ObjC grammar only, and its #include lines produce no import edge: whisper.cpp's coreml headers lost 4 (<stdint.h>, <os/log.h>). In .m / .mm files the gap has always been there: every #include in ObjC source produces no import edge.\n\nTo measure before changing: the import-edge delta on the ObjC corpus (AFNetworking, CocoaLumberjack, SDWebImage, fmdb, GPUImage, ResearchKit) and on mixed repos (whisper.cpp, sherpa-onnx), and whether any consumer (module linker, supply-chain tiers) keys on objc import edges."  # 030a
    fields: {}  # 030a
